End the CHECK-NOT search range at the start of the next match

The range searched by CHECK-NOT ended at the current file position, which
the following CHECK, CHECK-NEXT, CHECK-SAME or CHECK-COUNT had already
moved past its match. So the excluded pattern was also searched for in the
text of that match, and

    CHECK-NOT: foo
    CHECK: foobar

failed on an input containing only "foobar". LLVM's FileCheck searches only
the text between the two matches. CHECK-DAG and CHECK-LABEL followers
already computed the end separately and are unchanged.

Upstream: https://github.com/AntonLydike/filecheck (not yet submitted)
